[% PageVersion = 'Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-infra-ha-phase-a-registry-decomposition.tt,v 1.00 2026/08/10 shanta Exp' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %][% PageVersion %][% END %]

[% META title = 'INFRA-HA Phase A &mdash; Registry decomposed, role evaluated, port conflict resolved' %]
[% META description = 'Phase A of the Availability and Load Balancing plan gains its eight missing work todos (2037-2044); A.0 ROLE EVAL resolved to .199 on re-measured disk evidence; the planned registry port 5000 is corrected to 5001 because the live app container already holds 5000' %]
[% META author = 'shanta' %]
[% META date = '2026-08-10' %]
[% META roles = 'admin devops developer' %]

<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>INFRA-HA Phase A &mdash; Registry decomposition and role evaluation</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Planning / INFRA-HA (#202, sub-project #244)</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
            Phase A of the
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/K3S_APP_HA_PLAN') %]">Availability &amp;
            Load Balancing Master Plan</a> was tracked by a single gate todo
            (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=1905">#1905</a>) whose
            underlying work items had never been created &mdash; sub-project
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=244">#244</a> was empty.
            The eight A.0&ndash;A.7 items described in the plan text now exist as real todos
            (<strong>2037&ndash;2044</strong>), the mandatory A.0 role evaluation has been
            answered from fresh measurements, and a port conflict that would have blocked
            execution was found and resolved on paper before any container was started.
            <strong>No infrastructure was changed</strong>; this entry is planning and
            documentation only.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>A.0 ROLE EVAL &mdash; re-measured, and the hosts had swapped</h2>
        <p>
            The plan mandates that every phase evaluates its host on measured evidence and
            explicitly warns &ldquo;do NOT default to .199&rdquo;. Re-measuring on 2026-08-10
            produced a materially different picture from the 2026-08-07 figures recorded in
            &sect;3d:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>.199 workstation:</strong> load 1.80 / 8 cores, 22 GB RAM available,
                <strong>80 GB disk free</strong> &mdash; previously recorded as saturated at
                8.10 / 8 with 0 GB RAM free.</li>
            <li><strong>.126 production1:</strong> load <strong>8.89 / 2 cores</strong>,
                <strong>3.2 GB disk free</strong> &mdash; previously recorded as idle at 0.06.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            The CPU load profiles inverted within three days, which is itself the lesson: a
            load reading is perishable evidence and must be re-taken per phase rather than
            reused. The figure that did <em>not</em> move is .126's disk (3.5 GB &rarr; 3.2 GB
            free). <strong>Decision: the registry goes on .199</strong>, on disk headroom
            &mdash; 80 GB against 3.2 GB. .126 is disqualified on disk alone regardless of
            load. This lands on the same host the earlier retracted draft assumed, but by a
            valid route; the coincidence does not revalidate the old &ldquo;most powerful
            machine&rdquo; reasoning, and the decision is explicitly not transferable to the
            Phase B control-plane role.
        </p>

        <h2>Port conflict: 5000 was never available</h2>
        <p>
            The plan specifies the registry on <strong>port 5000</strong> in both &sect;3b and
            the Phase A section. On .199 that port is already published by the
            <code>comserv2-web-prod</code> container; 3000, 4000, 8081, 8083 and 11434 are
            likewise occupied. Freeing 5000 would require stopping a live application
            container, which standing operational rules forbid. The registry will therefore
            publish host port <strong>5001</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
            The durable mitigation is naming, not the port number. A registry's address
            becomes part of every image name, so an IP-and-port baked into tags propagates
            into compose files, manifests, deploy scripts and every node's
            <code>insecure-registries</code> list. The plan now mandates
            <code>comserv-registry.lan:5001</code> as the single canonical name, recorded in
            <code>services.json</code>, so relocating the registry later is a DNS change
            rather than a repo-wide rewrite. The plan also now warns that the
            <code>insecure-registries</code> value must match the image-name string byte for
            byte &mdash; an IP and a hostname are not interchangeable to the Docker daemon,
            and mixing them produces a failure that reads like a TLS bug but is not one.
        </p>

        <h2>&sect;8 blast radius corrected</h2>
        <p>
            The retained-SPOF list claimed that losing the registry means &ldquo;only new
            deploys stop&rdquo;. That understates it: a pod <em>rescheduled</em> onto a node
            without the image cached cannot start while the registry is down, so a node
            failure during a registry outage does not self-heal. The two faults compound.
            &sect;8 now states this, with the <code>docker save | ssh host docker load</code>
            escape hatch and the second-home requirement tracked in todo
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2044">#2044</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Todos created under sub-project #244</h2>
        <table style="width:100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: var(--spacing-medium) 0;">
            <tr style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.12);">
                <th style="text-align:left; padding:6px;">Todo</th>
                <th style="text-align:left; padding:6px;">Work</th>
            </tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2037">#2037</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.0 ROLE EVAL &mdash; answered, .199 on disk evidence</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2038">#2038</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.1 DEPENDENCY &mdash; not blocked; LAN-only HTTP needs no credentials</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2039">#2039</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.2 Disk headroom confirmed; growth estimate owed to A.6</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2040">#2040</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.3 Stand up <code>registry:2</code> on 5001 with <code>comserv2_registry_data</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2041">#2041</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.4 <code>insecure-registries</code> + canonical name &mdash; needs authorization on .126</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2042">#2042</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.5 Push/pull round trip with digest evidence &mdash; the gate</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2043">#2043</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.6 Retention / pruning policy</td></tr>
            <tr><td style="padding:6px;"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2044">#2044</a></td><td style="padding:6px;">A.7 Registry-down failover and escape hatch</td></tr>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>Still open &mdash; requires explicit authorization</h2>
        <p>
            Todo <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2041">#2041</a> (A.4)
            cannot complete without restarting <code>dockerd</code> on .126 so it picks up
            <code>insecure-registries</code>, and that restarts the live
            <code>comserv2-web-prod</code> container. That crosses the never-start-stop-the-app
            rule and must be scheduled deliberately with the user, not taken opportunistically.
            Gate todo <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=1905">#1905</a>
            therefore stays open until the A.5 digest round trip is demonstrated.
        </p>
    </section>

